{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\hist\\045.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Unit03", "conf": 0.847, "box": [[370, 63], [420, 63], [420, 81], [370, 81]]}, {"text": "Muslim Dynasties", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[420, 62], [527, 62], [527, 82], [420, 82]]}, {"text": "TheSeljuk(1037-1243AD)", "conf": 0.858, "box": [[61, 86], [386, 97], [385, 124], [60, 112]]}, {"text": "The Seljuk (taking its name from one of its chiefs,", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[59, 136], [539, 145], [539, 172], [59, 164]]}, {"text": "Seljuk) were one of the nomadic tribes of central Asia.", "conf": 0.902, "box": [[59, 164], [536, 172], [536, 198], [59, 190]]}, {"text": "Sharing a background of strong warrior tradition, Seljuk", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[58, 189], [539, 197], [539, 227], [58, 218]]}, {"text": "were a subdivision of the Kinig clan of the Oghuz Turks.", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[59, 216], [539, 225], [539, 251], [59, 243]]}, {"text": "In the 10th century they nomadized in the steppes to", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[60, 243], [539, 251], [539, 277], [60, 269]]}, {"text": "theeast CaspianSeaandnorthoftheAral Sea.Itwas in", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[61, 270], [540, 276], [540, 300], [61, 294]]}, {"text": "middle of 10th century that Seljuk and his followers", "conf": 0.946, "box": [[61, 295], [540, 301], [540, 328], [61, 321]]}, {"text": "embraced Islam. The Seljuk established a dynastic", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[61, 321], [540, 327], [540, 353], [61, 348]]}, {"text": "empire in the11th century.This empire expandedfrom", "conf": 0.895, "box": [[62, 347], [540, 353], [540, 379], [62, 373]]}, {"text": "Anatolia.to Punjab including most of modern-day Iran,", "conf": 0.915, "box": [[62, 372], [539, 379], [539, 406], [62, 398]]}, {"text": "Afghanistan, and Middle East. Seljuk died in 1007.", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[63, 399], [496, 406], [496, 429], [63, 423]]}, {"text": "Bythemid-1020s,the Seljuks crossingtheKaraKum", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[64, 439], [542, 445], [542, 468], [64, 462]]}, {"text": "Tower,a12th-centurymonumentsouth", "conf": 0.893, "box": [[556, 449], [808, 449], [808, 466], [556, 466]]}, {"text": "steppes reached Ghaznavid provinceof Khurasan.", "conf": 0.88, "box": [[63, 465], [496, 470], [496, 493], [63, 487]]}, {"text": "ofTehranin Iran commemorating", "conf": 0.88, "box": [[573, 466], [791, 467], [791, 490], [573, 489]]}, {"text": "Tughril Beg.", "conf": 0.78, "box": [[634, 487], [721, 487], [721, 509], [634, 509]]}, {"text": "Mahmud of Ghazna took.this movement as a", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[64, 510], [497, 516], [497, 539], [64, 533]]}, {"text": "Do You Know?", "conf": 0.852, "box": [[539, 526], [683, 526], [683, 550], [539, 550]]}, {"text": "danger.The Seljuks and Ghaznavids were involved", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[65, 536], [499, 540], [499, 563], [65, 559]]}, {"text": "in long power struggle over the region until Tughril", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[64, 561], [511, 565], [511, 590], [64, 585]]}, {"text": "TheSeljukmilitaryand state", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[536, 554], [771, 555], [771, 578], [536, 577]]}, {"text": "and his brother Chaghri, the grandsons of Seljuk", "conf": 0.915, "box": [[64, 586], [497, 592], [497, 615], [64, 610]]}, {"text": "governance systemswere", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[538, 583], [773, 583], [773, 604], [538, 604]]}, {"text": "defeatedtheGhaznavids..They", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[61, 612], [405, 616], [404, 639], [61, 635]]}, {"text": "the most advanced of their", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[538, 608], [774, 608], [774, 628], [538, 628]]}, {"text": "captured", "conf": 0.856, "box": [[420, 619], [496, 619], [496, 640], [420, 640]]}, {"text": "Nishapur,thecapital of Ghaznavid Khurasan.This", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[65, 638], [498, 642], [498, 665], [65, 661]]}, {"text": "time.", "conf": 0.765, "box": [[537, 632], [583, 634], [582, 656], [536, 653]]}, {"text": "ledtofoundationofSeljuk Empire.By1055,Tughril", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[65, 662], [507, 669], [507, 692], [65, 686]]}, {"text": "Beg conquered Iraq where Caliph gavehim the", "con